WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:06.939
Speaker 1: Speaking of anti vax, we actually
have some I think it's good news anyway.

00:00:06.939 --> 00:00:14.810
Remember that Wisconsin pharmacist who very
early on tampered with 500 doses of the vaccine,

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:16.420
making them unusable.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:19.460
He has now been sentenced to three years in
federal prison.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:20.460
This is good news.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.619
The only question is, should he have gotten
more time in prison?

00:00:22.619 --> 00:00:24.640
And I'll talk about that in a moment.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:31.109
CBS 58 is reporting that Steven Brandenburg,
the ex pharmacist, he is no longer a pharmacist.

00:00:31.109 --> 00:00:36.699
You will be glad to know the pharmacist convicted
of intentionally tampering with more than

00:00:36.699 --> 00:00:42.519
500 doses of the Moderna covid vaccine was
sentenced to three years in federal prison

00:00:42.519 --> 00:00:44.500
on Tuesday.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:49.579
Brandenburg was a third shift pharmacist at
Advocate Aurora Health Hospital in Grafton,

00:00:49.579 --> 00:00:54.850
where he admits to intentionally removing
dozens of vials of the Moderna coronavirus

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:57.449
vaccine from refrigeration.

00:00:57.449 --> 00:01:03.739
57 doses were administered to coworkers before
hospital officials found out about this and

00:01:03.739 --> 00:01:05.770
destroyed the rest of the doses.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:11.290
The 57 doses were determined to be still effective
and did not produce health effects for the

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:13.210
patients who received them.

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:18.590
At his sentencing, Brandenburg told the court
he was greatly ashamed of his actions and

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:20.790
he took responsibility for them.

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:25.340
His defense attorney detailed how his life
spiraled prior to the incident.

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:26.790
He had a messy divorce.

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:28.720
He had mental and emotional issues.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:33.649
He had a sense of disillusionment with work
and with the stress of the pandemic.

00:01:33.649 --> 00:01:38.649
But his former employer was very angry and
insisted he needs to be punished, that this

00:01:38.649 --> 00:01:43.509
has impacted hospital staff who are now just
trying to rebuild confidence in the system

00:01:43.509 --> 00:01:45.720
there that this won't happen again.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:50.270
Government prosecutors asked for fifty one
months, meaning four years, three months.

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:54.119
The judge said that the guilty plea.

00:01:54.119 --> 00:01:59.939
The lack of criminal record and other factors
led to a three year sentence that the judge

00:01:59.939 --> 00:02:03.530
feels is just but not excessive.

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:07.860
In addition to being imprisoned for three
years, the judge ordered Brandenberg to serve

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:13.140
three years of supervised release and to pay
about eighty three thousand dollars in restitution

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:14.340
to the hospital.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:16.720
Now, this is just the federal case.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:21.590
There is also a state case related to this
pending against Brandenberg.

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:22.930
We will see what happens there.

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:24.660
So first and foremost, three years.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:25.870
Is this enough time?

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:26.870
Um.

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:27.870
Yeah.

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:29.260
I mean, I guess so.

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:33.099
What I think about is.

00:02:33.099 --> 00:02:40.420
If indeed so, a bunch of these dosis 57 of
the 500 tambra doses were given to people,

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:43.120
but then the rest of the 500 were thrown out.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:44.970
This was really early on in the pandemic.

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:49.270
This was when there was really limited vaccine
supply and they were really only going to

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:50.270
health care workers.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:53.300
And those are the absolute, absolute highest
risk.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:59.780
So delaying four hundred and fifty doses,
443 doses, which was what just was thrown

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:07.690
out due to the tampering that realistically
could have led to some really high risk people

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:10.750
not getting their dose for a longer period
of time.

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:13.140
And some of them could have caught the virus
and some of them could have died.

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:15.409
Now, it may have happened or it may not have.

00:03:15.409 --> 00:03:17.190
I don't actually know whether that happened.

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:19.780
I don't know whether we can even say for sure.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:25.100
But people may have or could have died as
a result of this.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:28.010
And so three years, I don't know.

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:32.030
What I do know is these people have to be
made an example out of now.

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:37.930
You can always come in and say as as was argued,
this was a person who is not doing well emotionally

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:39.400
and mentally in all of the stuff.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:43.730
And clearly, those were mitigating factors
in terms of the sentencing.

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:49.730
But a signal has to be sent that this is just
an absolute no, this is I mean, would we say

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:51.920
it's equivalent to tampering with medication?

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:56.480
Would be is it equivalent to doing something
to a medication you're dispensing to someone

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:00.489
who may be seriously ill and depending on
a medication to stay alive?

00:04:00.489 --> 00:04:04.159
Would it be equivalent to messing with the
medication, doing something with it that makes

00:04:04.159 --> 00:04:07.599
